## Total cost

Two venue days plus 660 hotel room nights (220 rooms for 3 nights).

data total = city,total cost; Krakow,97720; Athens,116660; Prague,119480; Seville,131140; Lisbon,145900; Vienna,168340; Dublin,182440

chart hbar total unit=€ labels focus="Prague" title="Total cost for 220 people"

## Trade-offs

- Krakow is the cheapest at €97,720, but its largest room seats only 190, fewer than the 220 attendees. It is out.
- Athens is the cheapest city that fits, at €116,660, but the flight is 3.6 hours.
- Prague costs €119,480 and has a 2.0 hour flight.
- Vienna and Dublin cost €168,340 and €182,440.
- Lisbon and Seville have flights of 3.5 and 3.8 hours and cost more than Prague.

## Recommendation

We recommend **Prague**: only €2,820 more than Athens, with a flight 1.6 hours shorter.
